<title>JAPAN: Nintendo shares fall on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Nintendo shares fall on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nintendo Co Ltd fell in Wednesday morning trade on the Osaka Securities Exchange due to profit-taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0102 GMT, the shares were down 200 yen at 7,500 yen with turnover of 1.231 million.</p>
<p>Nintendo announced on Tuesday that it hopes to sell four million of its &quot;NINTENDO 64&quot; 64-bit videogame machines by the end of December in Japan and overseas.</p>
</text>
